We are a small team that advises small teams. Most of our clients employ between ten and two hundred people, and most of them call us when something has outgrown the way it used to be done.

## How we work

Every engagement starts with a week of listening. We would rather spend an afternoon to understand how the work really flows than a month to correct an assumption.

After the listening week, we write down what we heard and check it with the people who do the work. That summary becomes the shared starting point for the project. Nothing is decided in a meeting room that the team has not seen.

## What you can expect

- A named lead consultant from the first day to the last
- A written plan with weekly milestones
- Honest estimates, and a clear view of what we will not do
- Handover notes that your own team can use without us

## Our history

Harbor Lane started in 2012 with two consultants and one table in a rented room in Porto Celeste. Today we are a team of six. Most of our work is still done face to face, on site or in our studio, and we still keep a shared notebook for every client.

Meet the people on the [team page](/team/).
